    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "can you summarize the specific steps a company needs to follow when they receive a formal \"right to be forgotten\" request under GDPR? we need to make sure our internal process is compliant.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Upon receiving a formal \"right to be forgotten\" request, your company must first verify the identity of the requester to ensure they are the data subject. Next, you must conduct an assessment to determine if any legal obligations require you to retain the data, such as for legal defense. If no overriding grounds exist, you then have the obligation to erase the personal data without undue delay. Finally, you must inform any third parties to whom you disclosed the data about the erasure request.",
